Feature: Real-time Calculation of Inventory at Risk

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the data table is "f_inv_movmnt" in "agilisium_playground.purgo_playground"
    And the Spark SQL environment is configured
    And access permissions to Unity Catalog are granted
    
  Scenario: Calculate Inventory at Risk when DNSA flag is active
    Given the DNSA flag is "Y"
    When I retrieve the financial_qty from the f_inv_movmnt table
    Then I calculate the inventory_at_risk as the sum of financial_qty where dnsa_flag is "Y"
    And I display the inventory_at_risk
    
  Scenario: Calculate Percentage of Inventory at Risk
    Given the inventory_at_risk has been calculated
    And the total_inventory is defined and retrieved
    When I use the formula (inventory_at_risk / total_inventory) * 100
    Then I calculate the percentage_of_inventory_at_risk
    And I display the percentage_of_inventory_at_risk

  Scenario: Error handling for undefined total inventory
    Given the total_inventory is not defined
    When I attempt to calculate the percentage of Inventory at Risk
    Then I should receive an error message "Total inventory not provided. Calculation cannot proceed."

  Scenario Outline: Validate data retrieval and calculation accuracy
    Given the DNSA flag is "<flag_status>"
    And I have the financial_qty data: <financial_data>
    When I perform the inventory calculation
    Then the result should be <expected_result>

    Examples:
      | flag_status | financial_data                                   | expected_result |
      | "Y"         | [100, 200, 300]                                  | 600             |
      | "N"         | [100, 200, 300]                                  | 0               |
      | "Y"         | []                                               | 0               |

  Scenario: Data and pipeline validation for real-time access
    Given real-time data is required
    When the data is accessed through existing data pipelines
    Then the data should be current and reflect recent updates
    And any integration issues should be identified with a message "Real-time data access successful."

  Scenario: Security compliance and catalog access
    Given the Unity Catalog requires secure access
    When I try to access the data from f_inv_movmnt table
    Then I must comply with security protocols
    And I should confirm access with a message "Access granted to Unity Catalog."